---
title: 'Chocolate chip cookies'
description: 'Chewy American cookies, measured with cups and spoons the way the recipe card says it.'
category: 'Dessert'
makes: '24 cookies'
tags: ['american', 'cookies', 'baking']

portions: 24
---

## Dough ->&dough

[Whisk] In a #mixing bowl{}, whisk the @flour{2 cups + 2 tbsp}, @baking soda{1 tsp} and @salt{1/2 tsp + 1 pinch}. ->&dry ingredients{}

[Cream] In a #stand mixer{}, beat the @butter{1 cup - 2 tbsp}(softened) with the @brown sugar{3/4 cup + 1-2 tbsp} and the @sugar{1/2 cup} until ={pale and fluffy}, ~{3-4 min}.

[Add] Beat in the @eggs{2}, one at a time, then the @vanilla extract{1 tbsp + 1 tsp}.

[Fold] Fold the &dry ingredients{} into the butter mixture, then the @chocolate chips{1 1/2 cups + 50 g}.

[Rest] Cover and chill the dough for ~_fridge{30-60 min}.

## Baking

[Preheat] The #oven to ^{350°F}.

[Shape] Scoop the &dough into balls the size of a walnut onto two #baking sheets{2} lined with #parchment paper{}.

[Bake] Until golden at the edges but still soft in the middle, ~_oven{10-12 min}.

[Cool] Leave on the sheets for ~_{5 min}, then move to a #wire rack{}.
